hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2382","The narrator Sufyan says: That is, he did so while saying « » and « » . The narrator says: Then he came out with the leftover water from the ablution of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), so some people got that water and some did not, until a young boy inserted his hand from under the arms of the people and reached that water. Then Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) planted a spear in front of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) (the Prophet faced it and started performing prayer). Then it was not being forbidden for a donkey, woman, or dog to pass from the other side of it. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) led two rak‘ahs in the Zuhr prayer, and then continued to perform two rak‘ahs until he arrived in Madinah Munawwarah."
"2383","Abu Dharr said (and not the Prophet): If there is not anything like the back of a saddle in front of a man who is praying, then a donkey, a black dog, and a woman cut off his prayer. I asked him: Why has the black dog been specified, distinguishing it from a red, a yellow and a white dog? He replied: My nephew, I also asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the same question as you asked me. He said: The black dog is a devil. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 702)"
"2384","Abu Dharr said (and not the Prophet): If there is not anything like the back of a saddle in front of a man who is praying, then a donkey, a black dog, and a woman cut off his prayer. I asked him: Why has the black dog been specified, distinguishing it from a red, a yellow and a white dog? He replied: My nephew, I also asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the same question as you asked me. He said: The black dog is a devil. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 702)"
"2385","Abu Dharr said (and not the Prophet): If there is not anything like the back of a saddle in front of a man who is praying, then a donkey, a black dog, and a woman cut off his prayer. I asked him: Why has the black dog been specified, distinguishing it from a red, a yellow and a white dog? He replied: My nephew, I also asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the same question as you asked me. He said: The black dog is a devil. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 702)"
"2386","“The prayer is severed by a woman, a dog and a donkey.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 950)"
"2387","“The prayer is severed by a black dog and a woman who has reached the age of menstruation.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 949)"
"2388","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A woman, a"
"2389","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A donkey,"
"2390","I remember this about myself, I would be lying in front of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) in a way across, just as a bier is placed, and the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) would be performing prayer at that time."
"2391","“The prayer is severed by a woman, a donkey, and a black dog, if there is not something like the handle of a saddle in front of a man.” I (‘Abdullah) said: “What is wrong with a black dog and not a red one?” He (Abu Dharr) said: ‘I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the same question, and he said: “The black dog is a Shaitan (satan).” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 952)"
"2392","Abu Dharr said (and not the Prophet): If there is not anything like the back of a saddle in front of a man who is praying, then a donkey, a black dog, and a woman cut off his prayer. I asked him: Why has the black dog been specified, distinguishing it from a red, a yellow and a white dog? He replied: My nephew, I also asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the same question as you asked me. He said: The black dog is a devil. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 702)"
"2393","Once I came riding a she-ass when I had just attained the age of puberty. Messenger of Allah ﷺ was offering the prayer at Mina with no wall in front of him and I passed in front of some of the row. There I dismounted and let my she-ass loose to graze and entered the row and nobody objected to me about it. (Using translation from Bukhārī 493)"
"2394","I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Mecca and he was (at that time) at al- Abtah in a red leather tent. And Bilal stepped out with ablution water for him. (And what was left out of that water) some of them got it (whereas others could not get it) and (those who got it) rubbed themselves with it. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stepped out with a red mantle on him and I was catching a glimpse of the whiteness of his shanks. The narrator said: He (the Holy Prophet) performed the ablution. and Bilal pronounced Adhan and I followed his mouth (as he turned) this side and that as he said on the right and the left:"" Come to prayer, come to success."" ' A spear was then fixed for him (on the ground). He stepped forward and said two rak'ahs of Zuhr, while there passed in front of him a donkey and a dog, and these were not checked. He then said two rak'ahs of the 'Asr prayer, and he then continued saying two rak'ahs till he came back to Medina. (Using translation from Muslim 503a)"
"2395","I attended Fajr prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Masjid al-Khayf. When he finished praying, he saw two men at the back of the people who had not prayed with him. He said: “Bring them here.” So they were brought to him, trembling. He said: “What kept you from praying with us?” They said: ‘O Messenger of Allah ﷺ we had already prayed in our homes.' He said: “Do not do that. If you have already prayed in your homes, then you come to a masjid in which there is a congregation, then pray with them, and it will be a voluntary prayer for you."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 858)"
"2396","I asked: Why are you sitting while people are performing prayer? He replied: I have already performed the prayer, and the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) forbade us from performing any prayer twice in one day. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Amr bin Shu'aib himself is trustworthy; his narrations will be used as evidence when he narrates from someone other than his father. As for those narrations which he reports from his father from his grandfather, there is discontinuity and mursal (broken chain) found in them; for this reason, we do not use such narrations as evidence."
"2397","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Is there anyone who will give charity to him, such that he performs prayer with him?"
"2398","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will anyone give charity to him, by performing the prayer with him?"
"2399","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, led his companions in prayer. Then a man came, so the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Who among you will give charity to him by praying with him?"
"2400","I have not become a hypocrite. I will definitely go to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and inform him about this."" Then he went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! Mu'adh prays behind you, then returns and leads us in prayer. Last night, you performed the Isha prayer late. He prayed with you, then returned to us and stood forward, and began reciting Surah Al-Baqarah. When I saw this situation, I stepped back and performed the prayer alone. O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! We are people who work; we do our own labor (it is difficult for us to pray such a long prayer)."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Mu'adh! Do you want to put people to trial? You should recite such-and-such and such-and-such Surahs."" The narrator named Amr states: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had ordered him to recite short Surahs, but I do not remember their names. The narrator named Sufyan states: We said to the narrator Amr bin Dinar: Abu Zubair narrated this hadith to those people, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Sayyiduna Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him), ""You should recite Surah At-Tariq, Surah Al-Buruj, Surah Ash-Shams."" So Amr said: The words would be similar to this."
"2401","narrates: Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) used to perform the 'Isha prayer behind the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), then he would return to his people and lead them in this prayer. He was their imam."
"2402","narrates: Sayyiduna Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) (the narrator says) this is Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him). He used to perform prayer with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he would return to his people and lead them in prayer."
"2403","narrates: Sayyiduna Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) used to perform the 'Isha prayer behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he would return to his people and lead them in this prayer."
"2404","Umar ibn Muhammad al-Hamdani informed us: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us: from Ibn Ajlan: from Ubaydullah ibn Miqsam: from Jabir ibn Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) used to pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), then he would return and lead his people in prayer, praying that same prayer with them."
"2405","""What kept you from praying? Are you not a Muslim man?"" He said: ""Yes, but I had already prayed with my family."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺsaid to him: ""When you come you should pray with the people even if you have already prayed."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 857)"
"2406","""Ziyad delayed the prayer, then Ibn Samit came to me and I gave him a chair and he sat on it. I told him what Ziyad had done and he bit his lip (in disapproval), and he struck me on the thigh and said: 'I asked Abu Dharr the same question you asked me, and he struck me on the thigh as I struck you on the thigh and said: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the same question as you have asked me and he struck me on the thigh as I have struck you on the thigh and said: Offer the prayer on time, and if you catch up with them, then pray with them, and do not say: 'I have already prayed so I will not pray(now).""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 778)"
"2407","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Witr is a right; whoever wishes to perform five witr may do so, whoever wishes to perform three witr may do so, whoever wishes to perform one witr may do so, and whoever finds it difficult to perform it should recite it with gestures."
"2408","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Whoever reaches the true dawn and has not performed Witr, then he has no Witr."
"2409","I feared (the narrator is unsure, perhaps these are the words:) I disliked that witr would be made obligatory upon you.” (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The wording of these two narrations is different from each other, and their meanings are also different from each other, as these occurred in two different Ramadans in two different circumstances. It is not the case that the incident happened in the same month and in the same situation."
"2410","“Witr is Haqq.* Whoever wishes let him pray Witr with five (Rak’ah), and whoever wishes let him pray Witr with three (Rak’ah), and whoever wishes let him pray Witr with one (Rak’ah).” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1190)"
"2411","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Witr is a right. Whoever wishes to perform five witr, let him perform them; and whoever wishes to perform three witr, let him perform them; and whoever wishes to perform one witr, let him perform it; and whoever is unable to perform them, let him perform them with gestures."
"2412","Nafi' said: Ibn Umar used to lengthen his prayer before the Friday prayer and would offer two rak'ahs after it in his house. He used to say that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would do that. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1128)"
"2413","“I was with Ibn ‘Umar and I lagged behind and prayed Witr. He said: ‘What kept you?’ I said: ‘I was praying Witr.’ He said: ‘Do you not have the best of examples in the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?’ I said: ‘Of course.’ He said: ‘The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray Witr while riding his camel.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1200)"
"2414","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Whoever reaches true dawn (Fajr) and has not performed Witr, then he has no Witr."
"2415","I disliked this (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words:) I feared that Witr would become obligatory upon you."
"2416","""A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'O Messenger of Allah, how many prayers has Allah enjoined upon His slaves?' He said: 'Allah has enjoined upon His slaves (five) prayers.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, is there anything before them or after them?' He said: 'Allah has enjoined upon His salves (five) prayers.' The man swore that he would not do anything more or less than that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If he is speaking the truth he will most certainly enter Paradise.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 459)"
"2417","“I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Five prayers that Allah has enjoined upon His slaves, so whoever does them, and does not omit anything out of negligence, on the Day of Resurrection Allah will make a covenant with him that He will admit him to Paradise. But whoever does them but omits something from them out of negligence, will not have such a covenant with Allah; if He wills He will punish him, and if He wills, He will forgive him.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1401)"
"2418","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Five prayers and from one Friday prayer to (the next) Friday prayer is an expiation (of the sins committed in between their intervals) if major sins are not committed. (Using translation from Muslim 233a)"
"2419","When Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Muʿadh to Yemen, he said (to him), ""YOU are going to people of a (Divine) Book. First of all invite them to worship Allah (alone) and when they come to know Allah, inform them that Allah has enjoined on them, five prayers in every day and night; and if they start offering these prayers, inform them that Allah has enjoined on them, the Zakat. And it is to be taken from the rich amongst them and given to the poor amongst them; and if they obey you in that, take Zakat from them and avoid (don't take) the best property of the people as Zakat."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 1458)"
"2420","The next day, during the daytime, he performed twelve rak'ahs."
"2421","Salim b. 'Abdullah reported on the authority of his father that the Messenger of Allah (may peace be. upon him) used to observe Nafl (supererogatory) prayer on his ride no matter in what direction it turned its face, and he observed Witr too on it, but did not observe obligatory prayer on it. (Using translation from Muslim 700i)"
"2422","It was narrated from ‘Ali ؓ that The Prophet ﷺ used to pray Witr with three raka’hs (Using translation from Aḥmad 685)"
"2423","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) used to perform one rak'ah of Witr."
"2424","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to perform one rak'ah of Witr."
"2425","""We were with Sa'eed bin Al-'Asi in Tabaristan, and Hudhaifah bin Al-Yaman was with us. He said: 'Which of you offered the fear prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' Hudhaifah said: 'I did.' So Hudhaifah stood and the people formed two rows behind him, one row behind him and one row facing the enemy. He led those who were behind him in praying one rak'ah, then they went and took the place of the others, and the others came and he led them in praying one rak'ah, and they did not make it up."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1530)"
"2426","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked about the night prayer, so he said: One of you should continue to pray two rak‘ahs at a time, and when he fears that dawn is near, he should pray one rak‘ah, and thus make what he has prayed an odd number."
"2427","It was narrated from ‘Ali ؓ that The Prophet ﷺ used to pray Witr with three raka’hs (Using translation from Aḥmad 685)"
"2428","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to perform one rak'ah of Witr."
"2429","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Do not perform three rak‘ahs of Witr, perform five or seven, and do not resemble the Maghrib prayer."
"2430","How did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray during Ramadhan ? She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not pray more than eleven rak'ahs during Ramadhan and other than Ramadhan. He would pray four rak'ahs. Do not ask about their elegance and length. He then would pray for rak'ahs. Do not ask about their alegance and length. Then he would pray three rak'ahs. 'Aishah said: I asked: Messenger of Allah, do you sleep before observing witr ? He replied: 'Aishah, my eyes sleep, but my heart does not sleep. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1341)"
"2431","Between the time when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the night prayer till the dawn broke, he used to pray eleven rak'ahs, uttering the salutation at the end of every two and observing the witr with a single one, and during that he would make a prostration about as long a one of you would take to recite fifty verses before raising his head. When the mu'adhdhin finished making the call for the dawn prayer, he stood up and prayed two short rak'ahs, then he lay down on his right side till the mu'adhdhin came to him (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1336)"
"2432","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to recite Surah Al-A'la and Surah Al-Kafiroon in the two rak'ahs after which he would perform the Witr as the third rak'ah. In the third rak'ah, he would recite Surah Al-Ikhlas, Surah Al-Falaq, and Surah An-Nas."
"2433","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to separate between the even-numbered prayer and the odd-numbered prayer."
"2434","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to separate the even and odd prayers by saying salam in between them, which was done in a loud voice."
"2435","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) would separate the even and odd prayers by saying the salam aloud."
"2436","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform Witr and recite: ‘Glorify the Name of your Lord the Most High.’, [Al-A’la (87)] ‘Say: O you disbelievers!” [Al-Kafirun (109)] and ‘Say: Allah is One.”. [Al-Ikhlas (112)] (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1171)"
"2437","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray thirteen rak'ahs during the night, observing a witr out of that with five, he did not sit during the five except the last and then gave the salutation. Abu Dawud said: Ibn Numair reported it from Hisham recently. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1338)"
"2438","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to perform five rak'ahs and seven rak'ahs of Witr."
"2439","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) used to perform five rak'ahs of Witr, and he would sit only at the end of them."
"2440","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) used to perform five rak'ahs of Witr. He would not sit between these five rak'ahs. He would only sit at the end of them, and after sitting, he would say the salam."
"2441","""I said: 'O Mother of the believers! Tell me about the Witr of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' She said: 'We used to prepare his siwak and water for purification, then Allah (SWT) would wake him when He willed to wake him at night. He would use the siwak and perform wudu, then pray eith rak'ahs; not sitting until the eighth rak'ah, when he would sit and remember Allah (SWT) and call upon Him. Then he would say the taslim loud enough for us to hear.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1315)"
"2442","narrates: When the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) performed nine rak‘ahs of Witr, he would only sit after the eighth rak‘ah. Then he would praise Allah Almighty, mention Him, and supplicate to Him. Then he would stand up without saying salam, perform the ninth rak‘ah, mention Allah Almighty, and supplicate to Him. Then he would say salam aloud. After that, he would sit and perform two rak‘ahs."
"2443","“I asked ‘Aishah about the Witr of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said: ‘He prayed Witr at every part of the night, at the beginning, in the middle and at the end, when he died (he would perform it) just before dawn.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1185)"
"2444","The most beloved deed to him was that which was done regularly, even if it was little."
"2445","Make haste to observe the witr prayer before morning. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1436)"
"2446","I perform Witr and then go to sleep (i.e., I perform it before sleeping). The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: You have adopted the cautious way. Then he asked Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him): When do you perform Witr? He replied: I go to sleep, then wake up and perform Witr. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: You have adopted the way of a strong person."
"2447","Ghudayf ibn al-Harith reported: I asked Aisha: Have you seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ washing (because of defilement) at the beginning of the night or at the end? She replied: Sometimes he would take a bath at the beginning of the night and sometimes at the end. Thereupon I exclaimed: Allah is most Great. All Praise be to Allah Who made this matter accommodative. I again asked her: What do you think, did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say the witr prayer (additional prayer after obligatory prayer at night) in the beginning of the night or at the end? She replied: Sometimes he would say the witr prayer at the beginning of the night and sometimes at the end. I exclaimed: Allah is most Great. All praise be to Allah Who made the matter accommodative. Again I asked her: What do you think, did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite the Qur'an (in the prayer) loudly or softly? She replied: Sometimes he would recite loudly and sometimes softly. I exclaimed: Allah is most Great. All praise be to Allah Who made the matter flexible. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 226)"
"2448","""In the first rak'ah of witr, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite: ""GLorify the Name of your Lord, the Most High;"" in the second; ""Say: O you disbelievers!"" and in the third; ""Say: He is Allah, (the) One."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1700)"
"2449","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) say: Witr is not performed twice in one night."
"2450","Ubayy bin Ka'b said: ""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in Witr: ""Glorify the Name of your Lord, the Most High;"" and ""Say: O you disbelievers!;' and 'Say: He is Allah, (the) One.' And when he said the salam, he would say: Subhanal-Malikil-Quddus (Glory be to the Sovereign, the Most Holy) three times."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1729)"
"2451","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day apart from the obligatory prayers, Allah (SWT) will build for him, or there will be built for him, a house in Paradise.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1808)"
"2452","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Twelve rak'ahs, whoever prays them Allah will build for him a house in Paradise: four rak'ahs before Zuhr and two rak'ahs after Zuhr, two rak'ahs before Asr, two rak'ahs after Maghrib and two rak'ahs before Subh prayer."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1801)"
"2453","The Prophet ﷺ said: May Allah show mercy to a man who prays four rak'ahs before the afternoon prayer. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1271)"
"2454","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: I have performed prayer behind the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him). He used to perform two rak'ahs before Zuhr and then two rak'ahs after it. He used to perform two rak'ahs after Maghrib. He used to perform two rak'ahs after Isha. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: Sayyidah Hafsah (may Allah be pleased with her) informed me that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) used to perform"
"2455","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Two rak'ahs should be performed before every obligatory prayer."
"2456","'A'isha reported that the Apostle ﷺ was not so much particular about observing supererogatory rak'ahs as in case of the two rak'ahs of the dawn prayer. (Using translation from Muslim 724f)"
"2457","I never saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) perform any voluntary prayer more swiftly than this, nor did I see the Prophet (peace be upon him) seek any gain as eagerly as he would perform the two rak'ahs (Sunnah) before the morning (Fajr) prayer."
"2458","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The two rak'ahs before Fajr are more beloved to me than the world and all that it contains."
"2459","“I watched the Prophet ﷺ for a month, and in the two Rak’ah before Fajr he used to recite: “Say: O you disbelievers!” [Al-Kafirun (109)] and “Say: Allah is One.” [Al- Ikhlas (112)] (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1149)"
"2460","I consider it preferable that these two Surahs be recited in these two rak‘ahs."
"2461","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform two Rak’ah before Fajr, and he used to say: ‘The best two Surah to recite in the two Rak’ah of Fajr are: “Say: Allah is One” [Al-Ikhlas (112)] and “Say: O you disbelievers.” [Al-Kafirun (109)] (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1150)"
"2462","It was narrated from Ibn ‘Umar that when the dawn illuminated, the Prophet ﷺ would pray two Rak’ah. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1143)"
"2463","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was more particular about observing the supererogatory rak'ahs before the dawn prayer than about observing any of the other supererogatory prayers. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1254)"
"2464","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to perform the two Sunnah rak'ahs of Fajr briefly."
"2465","I would think perhaps he did not even recite Surah Al-Fatihah."
"2466","The Prophet ﷺ would pray two rak'ahs before the dawn prayer lightly so much so that I would say: Did he recite Surah al-Fatihah in them. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1255)"
"2467","""When the Muaddhin fell silent after the Adhan for the beginning of Fajr, he would pray two brief rak'ahs, then he would lie down on his right side."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1762)"
"2468","The Prophet ﷺ said: If any of you prays two rak'ahs before the dawn prayer, he should lie at his right side. Marwan ibn al-Hakam said to him: Is it not enough that one of us walks to the mosque until he lies at his right side? According to the version of Ubaydullah, he (AbuHurayrah) replied: No. This statement (of AbuHurayrah) reached Ibn Umar. He said: AbuHurayrah exceed limits on himself. He was asked: Do you look askance at what he says? He replied: No, but he dared and we showed cowardice. This (criticism of Ibn Umar) reached AbuHurayrah. He said: What is my sin if I remembered and they forgot? (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1261)"
"2469","I began to perform two rak'ahs at that time. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) took hold of my hand and said: Will you perform four rak'ahs in the morning prayer?"
"2470","The Messenger of Allah ﷺas saying: When the iqamah is pronounced for prayer, no prayer is valid except the obligatory prayer. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1266)"
"2471","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) kept looking at him, but did not object to him regarding this matter."
"2472","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whoever did not perform the two rak‘ahs of Sunnah of Fajr should offer them at the time when the sun has risen."
"2473","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him) that I remember this about the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessi"
"2474","The Prophet (peace be upon him) used to perform four rak‘ahs before Zuhr, two rak‘ahs after Maghrib, and two rak‘ahs after ‘Isha. At night, he used to offer prayer. I asked: Did he perform it standing or sitting? She replied: At night, he used to offer long prayers sitting, and he also used to offer long prayers standing. I asked: When he prayed standing, what did he do, and when he prayed sitting, then what did he do? She replied: When the Prophet (peace be upon him) recited while standing, he would also go into ruku‘ standing, and when he recited while sitting, he would also perform ruku‘ sitting."
"2475",": : "" "" "" "" : : "" "" . Abdullah bin Shaqiq narrates: I asked Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) about the prayer of the Prophet (peace be upon him): She said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) used to perform four rak‘ahs before Zuhr, then he would go and perform the (obligatory) prayer. Then he would return and perform two rak‘ahs, then he would go for the Maghrib prayer, then he would return and perform two rak‘ahs. Then he would go for the ‘Isha prayer, then he would return and perform two rak‘ahs. Then at night he used to perform nine rak‘ahs. I asked: Did he perform these sitting or standing? Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: At night he used to perform long prayers standing. I asked: When he recited standing (how did he perform ruku‘)? Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) replied: When he recited standing, he would go into ruku‘ standing, and when he recited sitting, he would perform ruku‘ sitting. After that, he would perform two rak‘ahs (sunnah) before Fajr."
"2476","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to perform a lengthy prayer before Jumu'ah, and after it he would perfo"
"2477","When any one of you observes the Jumu'a prayer (two obligatory rak'ahs in congregation), he should observe four (rak'ahs) afterwards. (Using translation from Muslim 881a)"
"2478","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When any one of you prays Jumu'ah let him pray four (rak'ahs) after that.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1426)"
"2479","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): \""When you begin to perform prayer after Jumu'ah, then perform four rak'ahs.\"""""
"2480","Messenger of Allah said: ""Whoever among you is to pray after the Friday prayer, then let him pray four."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 523)"
"2481","Messenger of Allah said: ""Whoever among you is to pray after the Friday prayer, then let him pray four."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 523)"
"2482","The Prophet ﷺ said: Prayer by night and day should consist of pairs of rak'ahs. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1295)"
"2483","The Prophet ﷺ said: Prayer by night and day should consist of pairs of rak'ahs. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1295)"
"2484","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) came to the people of Banu Amr on a Wednesday. He said: When you come for your Eid (i.e., on Friday), if you stay there and listen to my speech, that would be appropriate. They said: Certainly, may our parents be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah! The narrator says: When those people participated in the Friday (prayer), the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) led them in the Friday prayer, then after Friday he performed two rak‘ahs in the mosque. Before that day, he had not been seen performing two rak‘ahs in the mosque after Friday; before that, after performing the obligatory prayer, he used to go to his home."
"2485","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whoever among you wishes to perform prayer after Jumu'ah should perform four rak'ahs. If he is occupied with something, then he should perform two rak'ahs in the mosque and two rak'ahs at home."
"2486","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded us to perform four rak‘ahs after Jumu‘ah. The narrator named Suhail says: My father told me that if you do not perform four rak‘ahs in the Sacred Mosque, then perform two rak‘ahs in the mosque and two rak‘ahs at your home."
"2487","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to offer the two rak'ahs after Maghrib and the two rak'ahs after Jumu'ah only in his house."
"2488","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Two rak'ahs should be performed before every obligatory prayer."
"2489","""When the Mu'adhdhin called the Adhan, some of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ would get up and rush to the pillars (in the Masjid) and pray until the Prophet ﷺ came out and they were like that. They would pray before Maghrib and there was nothing between the Adhan and Iqamah."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 682)"
"2490","When any one of you observes prayer in the mosque he should reserve a part of his prayer for his house, for Allah would make the prayer as a means of betterment in his house. (Using translation from Muslim 778)"
"2491","I realized (what was happening) when I saw your behavior. O people! Offer your prayers in your homes, for the best prayer a person offers is that which he offers in his home, except for the obligatory prayer, for which the ruling is different."
"2492","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) entered the mosque and saw a rope hanging between two pillars. The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked: Whose is this? The people replied: This belongs to Sayyidah Zainab (may Allah be pleased with her). She performs prayer, and when she becomes tired, she holds onto it. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Untie it. Then he said: A person should pray when he is active and energetic; if he feels tired or his heart is not inclined, then he should sit down."
"2493","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) entered the mosque and saw a rope tied between two pillars. He inquired: What is this? The people replied: This is for such-and-such woman; when she performs prayer and becomes tired, she holds on to it. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: She should pray as long as she is energetic; when she fears that sleep is overcoming her, then she should go to sleep."
"2494","The Prophet ﷺ said: Prayer by night and day should consist of pairs of rak'ahs. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1295)"
"2495","“When anyone of you enters the mosque, let him not sit down until he performs two Rak’ah.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1012)"
